                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "236664994",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198054267963",
                            "num_reviews": 74,
                            "playtime_forever": 565,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 565,
                            "last_played": 1790902563
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Got this game for free as part of the Prince Jerian promotion. If I were summarize the reason I gave it thumbs dumb with one word it would be \"disappointment\". The first three chapters were really fun as you get to know the characters and worldbuilding. Starting with the 4th chapter things started to change. The game feels poorly balanced and many choices can require multiple stats/relations. In the 5th chapter you can barely do anything as most decisions requires 3+ stats/relations/destinies. It's too much and feels poorly balanced which leads to frustration. \r\n\r\nThe funny thing is they already have almost the perfect system to mitigate this: Willpower. If they just let you spend a proportional amount Willpower to overcome stat or relationship deficiency the game would feel so much smoother. Disappointed by the potential of the game and such interesting worldbuilding just went to waste.",
